/**
 * TASK: Read an object's private fields with reflection.
 *
 * snapshot(o) returns a Map from field name to that field's current value,
 * for every field DECLARED on the object's own class -- private ones included.
 *
 * The three moves you need:
 *   o.getClass().getDeclaredFields()  -- every declared field, any access level
 *   field.setAccessible(true)         -- unlock a private field for reading
 *   field.get(o)                      -- read the value (boxed, so int -> Integer)
 *
 * Skip synthetic fields (field.isSynthetic()); the compiler adds those and they
 * are not part of the object's real state. Field.get throws a checked
 * IllegalAccessException, so catch it (or declare it) inside your loop.
 *
 * Example, for a Sample built with ("gizmo", 7, false, 1.25):
 *   snapshot(sample).get("name")   -> "gizmo"
 *   snapshot(sample).get("count")  -> 7
